    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0602" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3584</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-21">April 21, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        25.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 138 of April
                    20, 1938<anchor n="21" xml:id="d592-f1"/> in which among other things the
                    Legation reported that the Fiscal Representative had been instructed by the
                    Haitian Government to proceed to the United States for certain purposes among
                    which was the inauguration of preliminary conversations with the Foreign
                    Bondholders Protective Council with a view to a new accord on the external loan,
                    I have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed an office <pb facs="0603" n="594"
                        xml:id="pg594"/> copy and translation of the instructions to the above
                    effect which the Minister for Finance wrote to Mr. de la Rue under date of April
                    19, 1938.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ferdinand L.
                    Mayer</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d592-a1.xml" xpointer="d592-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
